{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/118554","id":3525871469,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc7SKIdt","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118554","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118554.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118554.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118554","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/118554/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/118554/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118554/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/3883ba2a34f03eef28f4c290520da7eb8acaf45d","number":118554,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Wayland: Handle complex pointer event frames","user":{"login":"deralmas","id":31065808,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxMDY1ODA4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/31065808?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas","html_url":"https://github.com/deralmas","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Fixes #114436.\r\nFixes #114238.\r\n\r\nFrom [the spec](https://wayland.app/protocols/wayland#wl_pointer:event:frame):\r\n\r\n> The wl_pointer.enter and wl_pointer.leave events are logical events generated by the compositor and not the hardware. These events are also grouped by a wl_pointer.frame. When a pointer moves from one surface to another, a compositor should group the wl_pointer.leave event within the same wl_pointer.frame. However, a client must not rely on wl_pointer.leave and wl_pointer.enter being in the same wl_pointer.frame. Compositor-specific policies may require the wl_pointer.leave and wl_pointer.enter event being split across multiple wl_pointer.frame groups.\r\n\r\nFrom my understanding™ this means that a compositor SHOULD group leave/enter events together. Is this common? From my testing... Not really. Notably, (only?) KDE does this.\r\n\r\nOur pointer frame event assumed that we would be working with the currently pointed window but since all events must be logically grouped together I think it can really only group \"normal\" events related to the *leave* event.\r\n\r\nNow, whenever there's a pointer focus change, we send everything to the old window, if it exists, otherwise the currently pointed one.\r\n\r\nThis approach seems to handle complex event frames with both leave and enter events properly now, with good results on all compositors.\r\n\r\nThis patch also and makes it harder to get to a null check when the window simply does not exists (the error was meant only for existing but invalid windows), along with an helper method to aid in this.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nTested on:\r\n\r\n * sway 1.11\r\n * Weston 14.0.2\r\n * Jay 1.11.0 ([`a2e21cb`](https://github.com/mahkoh/jay/commit/a2e21cb926664cfc1980f8a38ec1aa34a7792c19))\r\n * KDE 6.5.4\r\n * GNOME 49.2.2\r\n * COSMIC 1.0.1","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279097326,"node_id":